; (string) The name of the database schema that stores the Slurm accounting data. The default is slurm_acct_db_ followed by the cluster ID from the cluster ARN, for example slurm_acct_db_a1b2c3d4e5f6 . Constraints: • min: 1 • max: 64 • pattern: [a-zA-Z0-9$_]+ SecretArn -&gt; (string) [required] The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager secret that contains the user name and password for the accounting database. The database user must be able to create the schema and to read from and write to it. Constraints: • min: 20 • max: 2048 • pattern: arn:aws[a-z\-]*:secretsmanager:[a-z0-9\-]*:[0-9]{12}:secret:.+ Shorthand Syntax: Eks={ClusterArn=string},Slurm={SlurmConfigStrategy=string,AccountingDatabase={Endpoint=string,Port=integer,Name=string,SecretArn=string}} JSON Syntax: { "Eks": { "ClusterArn": "string" }, "Slurm": { "SlurmConfigStrategy": "Overwrite"|"Managed"|"Merge", "AccountingDatabase": { "Endpoint": "string", "Port": integer, "Name": "string", "SecretArn": "string" } } }
